        "original_id": "3a0d322e-ce4c-5b7e-9599-036e52dd118f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Selfridges, Harrods, Jack O'Shea's\n- Places: Oxford Street, London, United Kingdom, Qatar\n- Topics: store size rankings, ownership, retail contracts, ethical code, foie gras\n\nFacts:\n- Selfridges opened its flagship store on London's Oxford Street on 15 March 1909.\n- Selfridges' flagship store on London's Oxford Street is the second largest shop in the United Kingdom after Harrods.\n- Harrods is owned by the state of Qatar.\n- Jack O'Shea's was formerly located in Selfridges.\n- Selfridges terminated Jack O'Shea's contract in 2012 after Jack O'Shea's broke the store's ethical code by selling foie gras.",
